<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Edeta</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Tossal de Sant Miquel</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Edeta was the chief town of the Edetani, an Iberian people, on the hill of Tossal de Sant Miquel above modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lliria">Llíria</a> in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valencia">Valencia</a>. Flourishing between the 5th and 2nd centuries BCE, it has yielded houses, a sanctuary and painted pottery showing warriors, dancers and hunting scenes, often with Iberian inscriptions. After the hilltop town was abandoned, the Roman town of Edeta grew on the plain below.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/edeta.jpg" alt="Edeta" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pelayo2 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:VGeneral_Liria.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
